cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Boundary-Mutation Testing for Pattern-Based Secret Detection"
message: "If you use this method or replication package, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mishra
    given-names: Shweta
    email: shweta.mishra.research@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  Replication package for boundary-mutation testing of pattern-based secret
  detection: a rule-level method that generates credentials from a detector
  rule's own regular expression, embeds them in a battery of realistic source
  contexts, and classifies outcomes at the rule level. Includes all harnesses,
  unmodified raw results, figure generation, a validated repair for the
  primary subject's defect (with a documented regression in a naive
  first-attempt fix), and a verified one-command reproduction for three
  scanners: GitHub Autopilot (commit 38b2013), Gitleaks 8.21.2, and
  TruffleHog 3.82.13.
keywords:
  - secret detection
  - credential leakage
  - mutation testing
  - metamorphic testing
  - regular expressions
  - empirical software engineering
license: MIT
